-- prompt_coherence(prompt): joint orientation + sense resolution.
--
-- NATIVE (src/prompt_coherence.c). The SQL body this replaces hung chat() for
-- every prompt -- >280s measured 2026-07-27 after the UD ingest -- and was taken
-- off the hot path in the same change that ported it. It was SQL doing what the
-- substrate law puts in C: set-returning functions as table sources (one
-- senses() per token, one bubble_up per candidate relation type), relation-name
-- identifiers split with string_to_array per row, and an O(n^2) join of 277-315
-- candidate senses against each other through an OR of both directions that no
-- consensus index can serve. Rewriting it as two indexed joins behind a
-- MATERIALIZED fence still measured 82s.
--
-- The C form is the same computation as a MEMBERSHIP SCAN: candidates fetched
-- once, then one indexed range read per direction with an O(1) hash probe per
-- edge. relation_rank and the canonical name come from the manifest in C
-- (laplace_relation_lookup), and the name's object token becomes a content id
-- through the same hash the substrate uses everywhere -- so no per-row SQL
-- function call survives anywhere in the read.
--
-- Returns, per prompt token, its best sense and the signals it was chosen by:
--   specificity  coherence / the candidate's OWN total rated mass -- THE RANK KEY
--   coherence    rated mass to the OTHER tokens' candidate senses
--   rel_mass     rated mass in a relation type another token NAMES (the
--                "what are the X of Y" shape, where X is a relation not a peer)
--   total_mass   ALL rated mass on the candidate -- specificity's denominator,
--                exposed for the electors' inverse-mass fallback (below)
--
-- RANK ON SPECIFICITY, NEVER ON MASS. Every mass-shaped scalar tried here has
-- elected function words, because they are wired to everything: denote_mu picked
-- the article and TZAR, highway breadth tied "a" with "pawn", and raw coherence
-- put `is`/`of`/`was` first on every prompt measured. The share of a candidate's
-- own mass that reaches the rest of the prompt is scale-free and separates them
-- cleanly -- measured on "What is a pawn in chess?": total mass a = 4.28e16,
-- chess = 5.28e14, pawn = 2.63e13, and pawn/chess elect correctly.
--
-- THE SINGLE-CONTENT-WORD LIMIT AND ITS SIGNAL (2026-08-01). A prompt with one
-- content word has no pair to cohere with: every candidate returns specificity
-- 0 and the election fell through to denote_mu, which favors function words --
-- "What is a glacier?" elected the article (denote_mu 1169.7 vs 1082.3) and
-- answered about the letter A. The per-token signal the earlier note said "does
-- not exist" was computed in this function all along, as specificity's
-- denominator, and discarded. total_mass is now a column: a function word's own
-- mass sits orders above a content word's (a = 4.28e16, glacier syn = 2.5e13),
-- so the four electors add INVERSE own-mass after peers and before denote_mu --
-- least mass first, non-positive mass last, firing only when every pairwise
-- key is silent. One election, one key order, unchanged as an invariant.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS prompt_coherence(text);

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION prompt_coherence(p_prompt text)
    RETURNS TABLE(ord int, tok bytea, synset_id bytea,
                  coherence double precision, denote_mu numeric, peers bigint,
                  rel_type_id bytea, rel_mass double precision,
                  specificity double precision, total_mass double precision)
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_prompt_coherence'
    LANGUAGE C STABLE;
